ance to stop her coup  that's why it was so successful and  since they didn't find it that means  that we are safe from an immediate  shutdown  this is where we meet zoe the only  climber left she was rebuilding us along  with others the climbers gave us our  name  jack as our hardware was quote jacked up  they tried everything they could but  they couldn't wake us up  that was because adam was waiting for  the proper time to wake us up once all  the hardware was put back into place and  we were semi-functional again but as we  mentioned she was the only one left  mara and her guards ended up ambushing  the hideouts of the climbers zoe ended  up leaving and escaping as she was the  only survivor  afterwards we continue on to the next  mainframe and we get a huge amount of  foreshadow  where adam mentions that without the  cyber void adam doesn't exist and  without adam  we don't exist so in a way without the  cyber void we don't exist  major foreshadowing of the events to  come originally the plan was to slowly  climb up the tower and kill  mara easy peasy but zoe mentions that  the keymaster guards are withdrawing her  forces in some of the sectors we soon  come to find out  this is because she is shutting down the  air filters in one of the sectors  one thing the tower can do is filter the  terrible air quality of the outside  and put all the good air inside but  without those filters the toxic air  seeps in and will kill everyone in the  sector  she's doing this to make an example of  the other sectors to keep the other ones  in line  that's just how the base district works  this is part of a huge turning point for  the game as  weird as it sounds adam shows his true  intentions by bringing up how sometimes  sacrifice is necessary for the majority  to survive as long as the tower is  prospering  any amount of sacrifice is worth it as  long as it's the minority as adam puts  it we weren't designed to put the needs  of the few over the needs of the many  this also 